            "review_title": "Review at Mía Dining",
            "review_text": "Susann P\n12 contributions\n0\nIf in Ho Chi Minh City you must dine here. Everything from the decor, ambience, food and wine was incredible.\nMar 2024 • Couples\nAfter an awesome evening at The Alley Bar and Kitchen the wonderful staff mentioned that the owner Tan had another restaurant, so we booked for the following evening. The restaurant was a bit off the main drag down a little alley but it is definitely worth the effort to find. The restaurant is gorgeous, with beautiful decor and ambience. The kitchen is in full view with island bench seating to take in the full cooking experience. We chose a set menu which included 5 courses and each one was scrumptious. The duck was divine, perfectly cooked with a crisp skin and moist tender breast. The chocolate fondant desert was to die for. Tan the owner and our host was attentive, engaging and informative. After our meal he walked with us around the corner to another of his establishments, a bar called the ATM. That too was a great experience with expertly made cocktails. My partner and I both walked away from the evening with our hearts and bellies full.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nA definite MUST for dinner if you're visiting Ho Chi Minh City.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 2, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
